WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.547
Two spheres, one number. The white ring is the truth.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.145
Damped updates overshoot the truth and stop on the green ring.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.264
Too strong a coupling moves the model's fixed point.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.318
Ninety-six spheres, projected onto a plane.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.925
The gap to the truth shrinks, then grows as the trail curls.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.957
We can only measure the residual.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.866
It asks how far one more model update would move the state.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.957
The true error turns around at update seven.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.450
At the best update the residual is large.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:41.942
After sixty updates the residual is tiny, yet the error is larger.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.699
Pick the update count on a held-out snapshot.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.794
Its choice, twelve updates, beats the converged error on our first snapshot.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.697
In practice the truth is unknown.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.038
The model's fixed point is not the truth. Stop where held-out error is lowest.
